## HandROM: A Real-Time RGBD System for Tracking Functional Impairments in Hand Motion

Accurate hand range of motion (ROM) evaluation is essential for remote monitoring of hand impair-
ments, including those caused by rheumatoid arthritis (RA), injury, or neurological conditions. This
paper presents a real-time, streaming-capable classification framework using the iPhone TrueDepth
camera to extract RGBD video of hand movement. The system integrates depth preprocessing, 3D pose
estimation with MediaPipe Hands, joint angle computation, and temporal classification using LSTM
models. We explore two dimensionality reduction strategies, PCA and Random Projection, and demon-
strate how jitter-based data augmentation enhances model generalization. The system is validated qual-
itatively against motion capture data from Qualisys. Results show that the best model using RGBD data,
PCA, and synthetic augmentation achieves a 93% classification accuracy and balanced F1 scores, sig-
nificantly outperforming RGB-only baselines. This work provides a clinically relevant, scalable solution
for telehealth applications.
